{
  "setupCommand": {
    "value": "npm install --legacy-peer-deps && (npm run build --workspace=web || true)",
    "evidence": "Ran it: exit 0. Plain `npm ci` fails (no package-lock.json is committed) and plain `npm install` fails with ERESOLVE (@types/react-dom@19.2.3 peer-requires @types/react@^19.2.0, web pins ~19.1.10). --legacy-peer-deps installs 453 packages in ~4m. The web build step is only there for codegen: it emits apps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts (untracked, not gitignored, absent from a fresh checkout) before failing, hence the `|| true`."
  },
  "verifyCommands": {
    "value": "npm run check-types --workspace=server\nnpm run check-types --workspace=web\nnpm run build --workspace=server",
    "evidence": "All three run and execute real work: server/web run `tsc -b` / `tsc --noEmit` (exit 1 and 2, pre-existing errors); `npm run build --workspace=server` runs tsdown and exits 0 in ~0.9s. Root `npm run check-types` (turbo) dies in this sandbox with 'failed to create directory /.turbo/cache: Permission denied' unless TURBO_CACHE_DIR is set."
  },
  "knownFailures": {
    "value": "No test suite exists in this repo - 0 tests, so 0 known test failures. Typecheck is red on HEAD before any change: 38 pre-existing TypeScript errors (server 2, web 36). Server: packages/api/src/features/exams/schemas.ts:70 (ZodDiscriminatedUnion.omit), packages/db/src/schema/auth.ts:1 (unused 'serial'). Web: 36 errors across 17 files, incl. src/utils/discriminatedUnion.ts (4), src/features/exams/components/ExamView.tsx (5), src/routes/dashboard.tsx (3), src/features/exams/stores/examStore.ts (3), src/features/exams/components/ExamGenerator.tsx (3), src/components/ui/form.tsx (3), plus verbatimModuleSyntax type-only-import errors in several files. `npm run build --workspace=web` also fails: src/components/ui/typewriter-loader.tsx imports 'styled-components', which is not a declared dependency.",
    "evidence": "Searched for *.test.*/*.spec.*/vitest/jest/playwright config and 'test' scripts across all package.json files: zero hits, no .github/workflows. Typecheck counts are from running the two check-types commands on HEAD after setup (routeTree.gen.ts generated)."
  },
  "devCommand": {
    "value": "npm run dev",
    "evidence": "root package.json scripts.dev = 'turbo dev'; README 'Then, run the development server'. Web on :3001, API on :3000 - not executed (host-only)."
  },
  "driveSetupCommand": {
    "value": "npm run db:start && npm run db:push",
    "evidence": "README 'Database Setup' (start Postgres, then `npm run db:push`); root package.json db:start -> turbo -F @my-better-t-app/db db:start -> 'docker compose up -d' in packages/db/docker-compose.yml - not executed (host-only)."
  },
  "driveStopCommand": {
    "value": "npm run db:stop",
    "evidence": "root package.json db:stop -> packages/db 'docker compose stop' - counterpart to db:start - not executed (host-only)."
  },
  "dbResetCommand": {
    "value": "npm run db:push",
    "evidence": "packages/db has no migrations directory and no db:reset script; drizzle.config.ts is push-based (schema ./src/schema). db:push runs `drizzle-kit push`, which rebuilds the DB schema from the schema files in the working tree - not executed (host-only)."
  },
  "notes": "INSTALL: the repo ships no lockfile, so the stock `npm ci || npm install` bootstrap fails twice over - `npm ci` for the missing package-lock.json, `npm install` on an ERESOLVE @types/react peer conflict. --legacy-peer-deps is required. node_modules was empty when this run started; installing it also creates an untracked package-lock.json (not committed).\n\nCODEGEN: apps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts is generated by the @tanstack/router-plugin vite plugin and is neither committed nor gitignored. Without it, `tsc --noEmit` in web reports ~6 spurious errors (Cannot find module './routeTree.gen', and every createFileRoute path 'not assignable to undefined'). There is no standalone generator CLI installed (@tanstack/router-generator exposes no bin), so the only ways to produce it are `vite build` or `vite dev`. That is why setupCommand runs the web build and swallows its exit code.\n\nTURBO IN SANDBOX: every root-level script (`npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run check-types`) goes through turbo, which here resolves its cache to /.turbo/cache and exits with EACCES. Cause looks sandbox-specific: .git is a gitdir pointer to /.sandcastle-parent-git/worktrees/..., so turbo's repo-root walk lands on /. Workaround that I ran successfully: TURBO_CACHE_DIR=/home/agent/.turbo/cache npx turbo check-types. The per-workspace `npm run ... --workspace=<name>` commands in verifyCommands bypass turbo entirely and need no workaround - prefer them. This should not affect a developer's own machine.\n\nNO TESTS / NO LINT: there is no test runner, no test files, no lint config and no CI in this repo. Typecheck and build are the only automated gates, and both are already red (see knownFailures). Two .stories.tsx files exist but no Storybook dependency is declared or installed, so they are typechecked as ordinary source and contribute errors.\n\ndriveEnv OMITTED deliberately. The variable name is certain (DATABASE_URL - apps/server/.env.example line 1, read by packages/db/drizzle.config.ts), but .env.example ships every value blank, so it gives no connection-string shape. packages/db/docker-compose.yml does define the dev database (POSTGRES_USER=postgres, POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password, POSTGRES_DB=my-better-t-app, port 5432, container my-better-t-app-postgres), so a per-branch URL would look like postgres://postgres:password@localhost:5432/my_better_t_app_{{id}} - but I would have had to invent the driver prefix and, more importantly, the matching clone step: Postgres runs inside the compose container, so createdb -T has to be tunnelled through `docker exec`, which the repo documents nowhere. Rather than auto-run a fabricated bootstrap on a real machine, both driveEnv and the per-branch database are left out; driveSetupCommand uses the shared dev database exactly as the README describes. Note also that apps/server/.env does not exist in the checkout - a developer must create it from .env.example (DATABASE_URL, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, BETTER_AUTH_URL, POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN, POLAR_SUCCESS_URL, CORS_ORIGIN) plus apps/web/.env (VITE_SERVER_URL) before the dev server will run."
}

